  "configuration_id": "config_015",
  "reason": "Evidence: All 9 completed experiments are multiprofile multimodal or single-modality baselines. The best config (config_049, scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer + weighted) reaches 0.725, but the incremental gain from switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 in the multimodal setting was only +0.013 (config_004→config_007), which is small and could be confounded by the image signal. Meanwhile, the rna_only baseline with pca_n2000 (config_029) sits at 0.591. Question: config_015 (rna_only, scvi_n200, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_029 (rna_only, pca_n2000, avgpool), isolating the RNA encoder effect without any image or fusion confounds. If scvi_n200 rna_only reaches ~0.68-0.70, the RNA encoder is the primary driver and further gains should target RNA representation; if it stays near 0.59, the image+aggregation pipeline is essential and we should prioritize image-side improvements. This is the highest-information experiment under budget because it decomposes the source of the 0.725 performance, directly guiding whether remaining experiments should focus on the RNA encoder, the image encoder/aggregation, or the profile setting."
}

